      "seed": 1021190589,
      "version": 233,
      "versionNonce": 1270677843,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785554534093,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Prevent conflicts by acquiring locks upfront.\n- \"FOR UPDATE\" clause lock every row the SELECT returns\n- A lock in this context is a mechanism that prevents other database connections from accessing the same data,\n until the lock is released. Databases like PostgreSQL and MySQL can handle thousands of concurrent connections,\n but locks ensure that only one connection can modify a specific row (or set of rows) at a time.\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Prevent conflicts by acquiring locks upfront.\n- \"FOR UPDATE\" clause lock every row the SELECT returns\n- A lock in this context is a mechanism that prevents other database connections from accessing the same data,\n until the lock is released. Databases like PostgreSQL and MySQL can handle thousands of concurrent connections,\n but locks ensure that only one connection can modify a specific row (or set of rows) at a time.\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
